course: dictionary
lesson: 12168
title: Compressed: squeezed, shorter, or smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compressed means pressed or squeezed into a smaller space, or made shorter or smaller. Picture a sponge pushed flat in your fist: it has been compressed.
explain: «The diver breathed from a tank of compressed air.» The air has been squeezed into a small tank, so the diver can carry enough air to breathe underwater.
explain: Compressed can also mean made shorter. «Mrs Hale gave us a compressed timetable, so every lesson was shorter.» In computing, «a compressed folder» has been made smaller so it takes less space.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in squeezed or made smaller. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Compress means to press or squeeze something into a smaller space.
fact: Compressed is the past form of compress, and it is also used as an adjective, as in compressed air.
fact: In science, gases can be compressed a lot, but solids and liquids hardly at all.
fact: In computing, a compressed file takes less space and downloads faster.
fact: Useful phrases: compressed air, compressed file, compressed into.
exercise: «The gas in the tank was compressed, so it fitted into a much smaller space.» What does compressed mean here? | Filled with bright colours | Spread out over a wide area | *Pressed into a smaller space | Made very cold and wet
exercise: «Ben saved the photos as a compressed folder so they would download quickly.» What does compressed suggest about the folder? | It is bigger and takes more space | It is empty | It is locked with a password | *It is smaller and takes less space
exercise: Which phrase describes a file made smaller for a computer? | a tight squeeze | compressed into a corner | compressed air | *compressed file
test: «The timetable was compressed into one short week.» What does compressed mean here? | Made longer and slower | *Made shorter, fitted into less time | Painted in bright colours | Lost for ever
test: Which word could replace compressed in «a compressed timetable» without changing the meaning? | sadder | longer | *shorter | louder
exam: In science, which can be compressed the most? | Liquid water | *A gas | A solid rock | A wooden table
